# Committed sources stay LF on every OS. The git hooks are sh scripts whose
# shebang lines break under CRLF, and privacy-check.js must read its own
# sources byte-identically across machines — a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true must not rewrite any of these.
#
# config.json, logs/, recon/, and .profiles/ are gitignored: git never
# applies any CRLF conversion to untracked files, so local data files are
# untouched by definition.
*.js     text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.aspx   text eol=lf
hooks/*  text eol=lf
